#lang r7rs/sweet
;; r7rs-lang-plan D1: `r7rs` brings its own reader and has no reader axis
;; (LangTraits.reader_axis_free = false), so a slash spelling is not a base
;; -- it is the same TUR-E0331 any unknown base gets, not a silent fallback
;; to the Scheme reader or to sweet-exp Turmeric.  `r7rs/sweet` is a
;; deliberate deferral (plan Section 8, Q5), and if it is ever wanted the
;; LANG_BASES[] table is where it goes.
(defn main [] : int 0)
